---
title: "Field Chief Technology Officer"
---

# Field Chief Technology Officer Job Family
The Field CTO serves as a strategic technical leader and trusted advisor to enterprise customers, helping them achieve their digital transformation objectives through GitLab solutions. In this capacity, they provide executive-level guidance on DevSecOps transformation initiatives, contribute to product strategy through field feedback, and serve as a technical thought leader both internally and externally. They work closely with customer technical executives to architect solutions while simultaneously building and scaling technical expertise within GitLab's field teams.

This role combines deep technical expertise in software development workflows, security, and compliance with strong executive presence and communication skills. Field CTOs play a crucial role in GitLab's growth by identifying strategic opportunities, driving new logo acquisition, and ensuring customer success through their DevSecOps journey. As they progress through the career ladder from Field CTO to Sr. Director, their scope expands from regional impact to global influence, with increasing responsibility for team leadership, strategic initiatives, and industry thought leadership.

## Field CTO

Reports to: Director, Field CTO or Sr. Director, Field CTO
Job Grade: 8

### Responsibilities

* Strategic Technical Leadership: Partner with enterprise customers to understand their technical vision and challenges, providing expert guidance on how GitLab can enable their digital transformation journey. Lead strategic technical discussions at the C-suite level and architect solutions that align with customers' long-term objectives.

* Industry Thought Leadership: Represent GitLab at industry conferences, write technical blogs, and participate in speaking engagements to establish GitLab's presence in the technology community. Share insights on industry trends and best practices in DevOps, digital transformation, and software development.

* Executive Business Development: Provide executive-level thought leadership on strategic opportunities for new logo acquisition and growth. Partner with sales leadership to develop technical strategies that address complex customer needs.

* Product Advocacy: Curate and manage field feedback while collaborating with the Product team on roadmap and issue prioritization. Contribute to product advisory boards and provide strategic input on product direction based on enterprise customer needs.

* Field Enablement: Scale and grow regional-level expertise within the field (SAE/AE, SA, CSM) through contributions to enablement and content. Develop and deliver training materials and best practices documentation.

* Customer Advocacy: Act as a prospect/customer advocate on DevSecOps transformation initiatives, providing guidance on implementation strategies and best practices.

### Requirements

* Significant experience with architecture of enterprise software development workflow
* Experience with software development tools, practices, and methodologies
* Experience delivering information/Cyber Security and compliance related solutions and assessments
* Strong verbal and written skills with demonstrated ability to articulate and communicate strategies to all levels in an organization (executive to staff engineer)
* Deep understanding of DevOps, CI/CD, and modern software development practices
* Strong public speaking and executive presentation skills
* Experience leading digital transformation initiatives
* Ability to use GitLab, including learning GitLab as part of the role
* Experience as CTO is a plus
* Advanced degree in Computer Science or related field preferred

---

## Director, Field CTO

Reports to: VP, Sales or VP, Strategy and Developer Relations
Job Grade: 10

### Responsibilities

* Strategic Program Leadership: Define and lead strategic technical programs across multiple enterprise accounts. Develop frameworks and methodologies for the Field CTO team to drive consistent value delivery across customer engagements.

* Team Leadership: Mentor and develop Field CTOs, providing guidance on complex customer situations and career development. Foster collaboration and knowledge sharing across the team.

* Strategic Growth Leadership: Drive executive-level thought leadership initiatives focused on new logo acquisition and growth opportunities across the region. Develop and execute strategic technical initiatives that expand GitLab's market presence.

* Product Strategy: Lead field feedback collection and prioritization efforts, establishing structured processes for product team collaboration. Partner with Product Leadership to influence roadmap decisions based on enterprise customer needs.

* Regional Excellence: Build and scale regional technical expertise through comprehensive enablement programs. Establish centers of excellence for DevSecOps practices and GitLab implementation.

* Transformation Leadership: Guide enterprise-wide DevSecOps transformation initiatives, developing frameworks and methodologies for successful customer journeys.

### Requirements

* Extensive experience architecting enterprise software development workflows
* Proven track record of delivering large-scale DevSecOps transformations
* Deep expertise in information/Cyber Security and compliance solutions
* Strong executive presence and ability to influence C-level decision makers
* Demonstrated success in building and leading high-performing technical teams
* Experience with modern software development methodologies and practices
* Exceptional communication skills across all organizational levels
* Proficiency with GitLab and ability to drive adoption
* Previous CTO experience is a plus
* Advanced degree in Computer Science or related field preferred

---

## Sr. Director, Field CTO

Reports to: VP, Sales or VP, Strategy and Developer Relations
Job Grade: 11

### Responsibilities

* Strategic Vision: Define and drive the technical vision for GitLab's enterprise customer engagement strategy. Lead the development of long-term strategic initiatives that position GitLab as a key strategic partner for enterprise customers.

* Global Technical Leadership: Lead and develop a global team of Field CTOs and Directors, ensuring consistent delivery of high-quality technical guidance across regions. Build a strong technical leadership culture within the organization.

* Enterprise Growth Strategy: Develop and execute global thought leadership programs focused on strategic growth and market expansion. Create frameworks for identifying and capturing new market opportunities.

* Product Vision: Establish global processes for field feedback collection and product influence. Partner with senior Product leadership to shape long-term product strategy and innovation initiatives.

* Global Field Excellence: Design and implement global programs for technical excellence and enablement. Create scalable frameworks for knowledge sharing and expertise development across regions.

* Industry Leadership: Drive industry-wide DevSecOps transformation initiatives and establish GitLab as a thought leader in enterprise digital transformation.

### Requirements

* Distinguished track record of architecting enterprise software development solutions
* Extensive experience leading global technical organizations
* Proven success driving strategic initiatives at Fortune 500 companies
* Comprehensive understanding of enterprise security and compliance landscapes
* Expert knowledge of software development methodologies and industry best practices
* Outstanding executive presence and communication abilities
* Demonstrated ability to influence product strategy and industry direction
* Strong understanding of GitLab and ability to drive enterprise-wide adoption
* Previous CTO experience is highly valued
* Advanced degree in Computer Science or related field required

## Performance Indicators

As with Got-To-Market roles, the Field CTO job family participates in a subset of the [Sales KPIs](/handbook/company/kpis/#sales-kpis).

- [Net ARR versus Plan (internal)](https://internal.gitlab.com/handbook/company/performance-indicators/sales/#net-arr-vs-plan)

## Career Ladder

The career ladder for the Field CTO role is not well defined and can take on many different paths.  Team members are encouraged to work with their direct manager on the next step in their career.

